parse`, `index`, `tail`, `verify`, `sweep` — a task's first (`done` 0, which is how a restarted digest check or sweep shows) and last reports at once, the rest at most once a slice, from `onSliceEnd`; `changed {rev, staged_version, issues_version, …ids, structural}` after every transition of a `ready` replica that changed something, which also restarts the digest check when an entity or the staged list moved. A delta whose digest disagrees, or a digest check that ends false, makes the replica `diverged`: the scheduler closes, so reads and edits posted meanwhile wait, and are answered from the replica the shell opens next (`close`, `open` … `end`, `adoptStaged` with what `staged` returned, `applyTail`). The method table (`METHODS`) is built from a few kinds, so the message handler has no per-method branch: `now` (answered at once, in any state — `open`, `chunk`, `close`, `staged`, `conflicts`, `setViewPlacement`, `dropViewPlacement`, and the artifact context: `setArtifacts {artifacts}`, `putArtifacts {changed, deleted_ids, staged?}` — the committed layer moves, then `staged`, when given, replaces the overlay — and `setStagedArtifacts {entries}`, each answering `null` and reading the whole call before the set moves), `later` (`end`), `read` (every `READS` name, a `scan` job when `readScans` says so; `getModelSummary` is handed the committed `rev` as `model_rev`), `evaluate` (every `EVALUATIONS` name, always a `scan` job over the ready model, the placements and the service's `ArtifactSet`), `inspect` (`stagedDiff`) and `transition` (`stage`, `unstage`: their params are read at arrival, so a malformed request is refused before it queues), plus the three replica methods above and the three that answer from the issue store, below. Reads, `stagedDiff`, `stage` and `unstage` wait in the model lane for `ready`, so an edit made during a re-bootstrap lands after the adopted batches. `stage` reads its ops through `readOps` and always asks the working copy to coalesce; it answer